    body: "The Ellora Caves sit roughly 30 kilometres from the city and the Ajanta Caves around 100 kilometres away, and both are UNESCO World Heritage Sites carved between roughly the 2nd century BCE and the 10th century CE. Alongside them, Bibi Ka Maqbara - often called the 'Mini Taj Mahal' - and Daulatabad Fort sit inside or near the city itself. This is not a passing tourist-brochure fact: it supports a real, ongoing local employment layer in licensed heritage tour-guiding, hotel and hospitality operations built around a steady inbound-tourist flow, and conservation-adjacent work connected to the Archaeological Survey of India's presence at these sites - a genuine career direction with essentially no equivalent on any other city page here.",
  },
  {
    title: "Paithan's handloom-sari economy adds a craft-heritage income layer most outsiders never connect to Aurangabad",
    body: "Paithan, a town roughly 50 kilometres from Aurangabad on the banks of the Godavari near the Jayakwadi Dam, has given its name to the Paithani sari - a handwoven silk sari tradition recognised nationally as one of India's finest, still produced by weaver families in the region. It is a smaller, more specialised economy than the auto-pharma cluster or the heritage-tourism circuit, but it is a real one, and for someone from a weaving or craft-adjacent family, deciding whether to build on that traditional skill, move toward a design or textile-marketing direction built on it, or step away from it entirely toward an unrelated professional path is a genuine decision worth naming rather than ignoring.",
  },
];

const marathwadaForkItems = [
  {
    title: "Family farm-income pressure versus a professional or salaried skill path",
    listItems: [
      "A poor monsoon, a crop-price crash, or a bad cotton or sugarcane season can wipe out a year's household income overnight in ways a salaried role in Aurangabad's industrial or services economy does not",
      "That pressure is real and pushes many Aurangabad and wider-Marathwada families to want the next generation on a stable, skill-based income path, not because farming is looked down on, but because its income is genuinely less predictable",
      "The honest next step is building a high-value skill portfolio deliberately aimed at that stability, rather than assuming any degree automatically delivers it",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Waluj-Chikalthana's auto-ancillary and pharma cluster versus a metro move",
    listItems: [
      "Bajaj Auto's Waluj plant, Endurance Technologies, and the pharmaceutical manufacturing units run by Wockhardt and Lupin are genuine, stable local employers across engineering, quality, production, and pharma-manufacturing roles",
