      "Getting this specific fit right - rather than assuming either 'Aurangabad has nothing' or 'the industrial belt covers every skill' - is what actually moves someone toward unlocking high income opportunities sooner",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "The Ajanta-Ellora heritage-tourism economy as a genuine third path, not a fallback",
    listItems: [
      "Licensed tour-guiding, hospitality and hotel operations, and conservation-adjacent research or archival work around Ajanta, Ellora, Daulatabad, and Bibi Ka Maqbara form a real, if smaller and more seasonal, career layer specific to this city",
      "It suits a genuinely different skill set - language ability, historical and cultural depth, hospitality service skills, or conservation-science interest - than either the farm-to-professional shift or the auto-pharma manufacturing track",
      "Weighing it honestly against the other two paths, rather than treating it as a hobby interest, is part of getting a real Aurangabad decision right",
    ],
  },
];

const aurangabadAreaItems = [
  {
    title: "Waluj and Chikalthana carry Aurangabad's manufacturing and pharma economy",
