  },
  {
    title: "Cidco-N and Garkheda reflect the city's newer, more professional residential growth",
    body: "The Cidco (City and Industrial Development Corporation) sectors and Garkheda, developed from the 1970s onward as Aurangabad's planned residential extension, house much of the city's newer professional and salaried-family population, often with closer ties to Waluj-Chikalthana employment or to Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Marathwada University than to the old city's trading economy.",
  },
  {
    title: "The old city around Kranti Chowk, Nirala Bazar, and Paithan Gate carries Aurangabad's historic commerce and Bibi Ka Maqbara's precinct",
    body: "Kranti Chowk sits at the heart of the city's commercial core, with Nirala Bazar and the Paithan Gate area carrying older trading and small-business activity, and Bibi Ka Maqbara's Mughal-era mausoleum standing close by. Families rooted in this part of the city are often weighing an existing family trade or business against a shift toward the industrial belt, a salaried professional path, or heritage-tourism-linked work in the same historic precinct.",
