    title: "Should I search for career counselling in Aurangabad or Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar - does the renamed city change anything about the guidance?",
    body: "No. The city was officially renamed Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar in 2023, but 'Aurangabad' remains the name most people still search, use in conversation, and recognise on official documents and addresses issued before the change. The guidance itself, the local economy, and the decisions in front of you are exactly the same whichever name you use - this page and the counselling process treat both as the same city.",
  },
  {
    title: "My family depends on farm income and wants me settled in a stable job - how does counselling actually help with that specific pressure?",
    body: "That pressure is real and common across Marathwada, and it deserves a direct answer rather than generic 'follow your passion' advice. Good counselling should map your specific aptitude and interests against Aurangabad's actual stable-income paths - the Waluj-Chikalthana industrial and pharma cluster, a services or administrative role, or further study - and help you build the skill direction that gets you there, rather than assuming any single degree automatically delivers stability.",
  },
  {
    title: "Is it worth building a career around Bajaj Auto's plant or the pharma companies here, or should I aim for Pune or Mumbai instead?",
    body: "Both can be right, depending on your specific skill direction. Waluj and Chikalthana's auto-ancillary and pharmaceutical-manufacturing base offers genuine engineering, quality, and production roles, but it is a narrower slice of the economy than Pune's or Mumbai's much larger industrial and services markets. The honest answer depends on whether your specific skill fits what this local cluster is actually hiring for right now, not on assuming either city is automatically the better bet.",
  },
  {
    title: "Is a tour-guiding or hospitality career around Ajanta and Ellora a real path, or just seasonal work?",
    body: "It is a genuine, if smaller and more seasonal, career layer specific to Aurangabad's heritage-tourism economy - licensed guiding, hotel and hospitality operations, and conservation-adjacent roles connected to two UNESCO World Heritage Sites in the same district. Whether it suits you depends on your own language ability, service orientation, and interest in cultural and historical depth, which is exactly the kind of fit a real counselling conversation should help you test honestly, rather than dismissing it or overselling it.",
  },
  {
    title: "Does a degree from Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Marathwada University or a local Aurangabad college carry less weight outside the city?",
    body: "A degree's real weight comes from the institution's own standing and the skills and proof of work you build alongside it, not from being based in a Marathwada city rather than a metro. Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Marathwada University and the Government College of Engineering, Aurangabad, are recognised on their own merit. What matters more when competing for roles outside Aurangabad's own industrial and services base is pairing that degree with a genuinely deliberate, high-value skill portfolio rather than the degree alone.",
  },
];

const deliverableItems = [
